  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">222127_FY24 #9_UNICEF_Bangladesh_Nutrition Cox&apos;s Bazaar</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Specific Objective 1: By December 2024, Nutrition service providers are capacitated to provide comprehensive maternal, child and adolescent nutrition service package in Rohingya refugee camps (5,6,8W &amp; 10) 
 
 Specific Objective 2: By December 2024, the community-based nutrition programme is strengthened to improve the coverage and quality of maternal, child, and adolescent nutrition, micronutrient supplementation 
 
 Specific Objective 3: By December 2024, cases of severe acute malnutrition (SAM) are effectively managed through the community and facility-based management of severe acute malnutrition in Rohingya Refugee camps (5,6,8W &amp; 10) 
 
 Specific Objective 4: By December 2024, children, adolescents and PLW have access to adequate supplementation for the prevention of micronutrient deficiencies in Rohingya Refugee Camps (5,6,8W &amp;10) 
 
 Specific Objective 5: By December 2024, the affected population benefit from malnutrition treatment and prevention services in the Rohingya refugee camps during emergency situations</narrative>
  </description>
